Subject: [PATCH v11 07/10] jails/instances/lab-mail: Take posts with OpenSMTPD
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: qnuuzmntpryrvxvlnxrkumrlulzwtmmx
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:21:17 +0000

smtprelay relays each post to Fastmail, so a post reaches the list
only by a round trip through Fastmail, and posting fails whenever
Fastmail does. OpenSMTPD hands a post straight to Dovecot, and holds
it in its queue while Dovecot is down. Nothing posted leaves lab-mail
except through the sync, so the Fastmail app password no longer needs
SMTP access, and mbsync is left as its only reader.

- OpenSMTPD takes posts on loopback and hands mail for the list to
  Dovecot over LMTP. It discards copies to the known addresses, and
  refuses any other recipient while the client is connected.
- OpenSMTPD's own parser refuses a header it cannot read, and adds a
  missing Message-ID and Date, as the spec asks.
- LMTP delivers each post to INBOX, and the next sync carries it to
  Fastmail.
- smtprelay, jq, and the mailcred group are removed.
- check covers OpenSMTPD, its queue, and that only mbsync can read
  mail-creds.
